Entities

This directory contains all entity classes for the application.

Entities represent the domain models of your application and are responsible for:
- Storing data for a single object (e.g., User, Message, Product)
- Providing getters and setters for properties
- Optionally providing simple validation or utility methods
- Being independent of the database layer

Entities should not perform SQL queries or handle HTTP requests. Those responsibilities belong to DAOs, Services, or Controllers.

-----------------------------
Entities Structure

- Each entity class represents a single domain object.
- All entity classes are inside the App\Entities namespace.
- Properties are typically private or protected with getter and setter methods.
-  Can include type hints and strict types (declare(strict_types=1);).